hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1055","'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said, When someone enters a house which is not lived in"
"1056","He told us Ishaq, he said: Ali bin al-Husain told us, he said: My father told me, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: ""Do not enter homes other than your own until you have made sure and have given your greetings to the inhabitants."" He then specified this, saying: ""It is no sin for you to enter homes other than those that are inhabited, provided there is enjoyment for you and Allah knows what you bring and what you hide."""
"1057","Regarding the ayat, Those you own as slaves should ask your permission to enter"" (24:56)"
"1058","Ibn 'Umar reported that when his children had reached puberty and he had withdrawn to his room, none of them entered where he was except with his permission."
"1059","'Alqama said, A man came to 'Abdullah and said"
"1060","Muslim ibn Nadhir said, A man asked Hudhayfa"
"1061","Musa ibn Talha said, I entered where my mother was with my father. He went in and I followed him. He turned and pushed me in the chest so that I fell on my bottom. Then he said"
"1062","Jabir said, A man should ask permission from his son and his mother"
"1063","before the Dawn Prayer and when you have undressed at noon and after the Night Prayer - three times of nakedness for you.' (24:56) Ibn 'Abbas said, 'He did not command these individuals to ask permission other than at these three times of nakedness.' Then he went on to say, 'The verse in Surat an-Nur:57 is: 'Once your children have reached puberty, they should ask your permission to enter as those before them also asked permission.'""1064"""
"1064","Qutaybah narrated to us, saying: Abdthar narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from Kurdus, from Abdullah, who said: A man seeks permission to enter upon his father, his mother, his brother, and his sister."
"1065","'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr reported that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari asked permission of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, but he did not grant him permission. It seemed that he was busy. Abu Musa came back and 'Umar had finished. He said, Didn't I hear the voice of 'Abdullah ibn Qays? Give him permission to enter."" He was told"
"1066","Regarding the person who asks for permission to enter before he gives the greeting, Abu Hurayra said, He is not given permission until he has first given the greeting."""
"1067","Abu Hurayra said, When someone comes in and does not say"
"1068","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, If a man looks into your house and you take some pebbles and gouge out his eye"
"1069","Our narrator Hajjaj said: Our narrator Hammad said: Our narrator Ishaq bin Abdullah said: Anas said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was standing and praying, when a man looked into his house, took an arrow from his quiver, and shot it in the direction of his eyes."
"1070","Sahl ibn Sa'd told him that a man looked from a room through the door of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, had a comb with which he was scratching his hair. When the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, saw him, he said, If I had known that you were looking at me"
"1071","Anas said, A man looked through a gap into the room of the Prophet"
"1072","Anas said, A man looked through a gap into the room of the Prophet"
"1073","'Ubayd ibn Hunayn related to him that Abu Musa said, I asked permission three times to come in to 'Umar"
"1074","'Abdullah said, When a man is given an invitation"
"1075","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When one of you gives someone an invitation and the person you invited comes with your messenger"
"1076","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, A man's messenger to another man is his permission to enter."""
"1077","Musa bin Isma'il narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, saying: 'Asim narrated to us, saying: Muhammad narrated to us from Abu al-'Alaniya, saying: I visited Abu Sa'id al-Khudi, and I greeted him, but he did not respond to me. Then I greeted him again, but he did not respond to me. Then I greeted him a third time, and I raised my voice and said, ""As-salamu 'alaykum, ya ahli al-dari,"" but he did not respond to me. So I became despondent and sat down. Then a young boy came out and said, ""Enter."" So I entered, and Abu Sa'id said to me, ""If you had added [something], they would have responded to you."" So I asked him about the prohibited things, and he did not tell me about anything except that it was haraam. Then I asked him about the forehead, and he said, ""Haram."" Muhammad said: A black mole will be placed on his forehead, and he will be punished."
"1078","'Abdullah ibn Busr, the Companion of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said that when the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, came to a door when he wanted to ask permission to enter, he did not face it directly. He stood to the right or the left. If he was given permission, he went in. Otherwise he went away."
"1079","Abdullah bin Salah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Shurayh narrated to me, Abdullah bin Muawiya bin Hudayj narrated to me from his father, saying: I visited Umar bin al-Khatab, may Allah be pleased with him, and I asked permission to enter, and they said to me: ""Make room until he comes out to you."" So I sat near his door, and he came out to me, called for water, performed ablution, then wiped his shoes, and said: ""O Commander of the Believers, is this a matter of fate or something else?"" He said: ""It is a matter of fate, or it is not."""
"1080","Anas ibn Malik reported that people knocked on the door of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, using their fingernails."
"1081","Kalda ibn Hanbal reported that Safwan ibn Umayya sent him to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, during the Conquest of Makka with some milk, gazelle, and cucumber. (Abu 'Asim said that the meant vegetables.) The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was at the top of the valley and I did not give the greeting nor ask for permission. He said, Go back and say"
"1082","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, If someone looks inside"
"1083","'Ata' reported that Abu Hurayra said, When someone says"
"1084","Rib'i ibn Hirash reported that a man of the Banu 'Amir came to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, Can I come in?"" The Prophet"
"1085","Ibn 'Abbas said, \'Umar asked permission to visit the Prophet"
"1086","Jabir said, I came to the Messenger of Allah"
"1087","Burayda said, The Messenger of Allah"
"1088","'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn Ju'dan said, I was with 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar and he asked permission from the people of the house to enter. He was told"
"1089","Abu Hurayra said, The Messenger of Allah"
"1090","Muslim ibn Nadhir said, A man asked permission to enter from Hudhayfa. He looked in and said"
"1091","Anas ibn Malik reported that a bedouin came to the house of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and put his eye to the crack of the door. Therefore the Prophet took an arrow or a sharp stick and aimed it at the bedouin as to gouge out his eye. The man left and the Prophet said, If you had stayed"
"1092","'Umar ibn al-Khattab said, Anyone who fills his eye with the contents of a house before he has been given permission has gone astray."""
"1093","Thawban, the mawla of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, related that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, It is not lawful for a Muslim man to look inside a house until he has been given permission. If he does so"
"1094","if they live, they will have enough, and if they die, they will enter the Garden. Allah Almighty is responsible for whoever enters his house , saying 'Peace'. Allah is responsible for whoever goes out to the mosque. Allah is responsible for whoever goes out in the Way of Allah.""1095"""
"1095","Muhammad ibn Muqatil narrated to us, saying: Abdullah informed us, saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir saying: ""When you enter upon your family, greet them with a greeting from Allah, blessed and good."""
"1096","Jabir reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, When a man enters his house"
"1097","A'yan al-Khwarizmi said, We came to Anas ibn Malik while he was sitting his foyer with anyone else with him. My companion greeted him and said"
"1098","'Ata' said, Ibn 'Umar used to ask permission to enter market-stalls."""
"1099","'Ata' said, Ibn 'Umar used to ask permission to enter market-stalls."""
"1100","Abu Abdul Malik, the mawla of Umm Miskin, the daughter of ('Umar) ibn 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, said, My mistress sent me to Abu Hurayra and he came with me. When he was at the door"
"1101","Abu 'Uthman an-Nahdi said, Abu Musa wrote to a Persian grandee and greeted him in his letter. He was asked"
"1102","Abu Basra al-Ghifari reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, I will ride to the Jews tomorrow. Do not give them the greeting first. If they greet you"
"1103","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, Do not give the People of the Book the greeting first. Force them to the narrowest part of the road."""
"1104","'Alqama said, \'Abdullah used to greet the Persian grandees with a gesture."""
"1105","Anas said, A Jew passed by the Prophet"
